From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 21:17:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] libril: match the vendor blob's nanopb field layout (16-bit)

nanopb decides sizeof(pb_field_t) at compile time via PB_FIELD_8/16/32BIT, and libril is where that
choice lands for the whole RIL: QTI's libril-qc-qmi-1.so imports pb_encode/pb_decode from libril
rather than carrying its own copy.

AOSP builds libril with PB_FIELD_32BIT. The msm8992 blob was built against the 16-bit layout, so the
descriptor arrays it hands to pb_encode are strided wrong and the encoder walks off the end:

  #00 libril.so (encode_field+364)
  #01 libril.so (pb_encode+76)
  #02 libril-qc-qmi-1.so (qcril_qmi_encode_npb+64)
  #03 libril-qc-qmi-1.so (qcril_qmi_ims_pack_msg+1936)
  #06 qcril_qmi_imsa_service_status_ind_hdlr

It only reproduces once something connects to the IMS socket, because rild never packs an IMS message
otherwise -- so every build without a working ims.apk looked healthy. With 32-bit, rild SIGSEGVs every
~5s (27 restarts in 145s) and telephony cycles; with 16-bit it is stable at one start and IMS
registers.

---
 libril/Android.mk | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libril/Android.mk b/libril/Android.mk
index c39c5a9..7b71418 100644
--- a/libril/Android.mk
+++ b/libril/Android.mk
@@ -24,11 +24,16 @@ LOCAL_SHARED_LIBRARIES := \
     android.hardware.radio@1.1 \
     libhidlbase \
 
+# nanopb's pb_field_t layout is decided at COMPILE time by PB_FIELD_8/16/32BIT, and libril is where
+# it lands: QTI's libril-qc-qmi-1.so imports pb_encode/pb_decode from here rather than carrying its
+# own. A 2016 blob built against one layout, handed descriptors to an encoder built with another,
+# walks off the end of the field array -- rild SIGSEGVs in encode_field the first time an IMS socket
+# client exists to send to. Match the blob, not the AOSP default.
 LOCAL_STATIC_LIBRARIES := \
-    libprotobuf-c-nano-enable_malloc-32bit \
+    libprotobuf-c-nano-enable_malloc-16bit \
 
 LOCAL_CFLAGS += -Wall -Wextra -Wno-unused-parameter -Werror
-LOCAL_CFLAGS += -DPB_FIELD_32BIT
+LOCAL_CFLAGS += -DPB_FIELD_16BIT
 
 ifeq ($(SIM_COUNT), 2)
     LOCAL_CFLAGS += -DANDROID_MULTI_SIM -DDSDA_RILD1
